<title>USA: Hewlett-Packard unveils color copiers.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard unveils color copiers.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co, already the leader in the computer printer market, on Tuesday unveiled its new personal color copiers, which are expected to start at about $699.</p>
<p>HP said its strategy is to prompt customers to switch from monochrome personal copiers and retail copy centers by offering affordable desktop color copiers based on HP's popular inkjet technology.</p>
<p>The company gave no details on how many versions of the stand-alone copiers it would begin to sell, or what the price range of the line would be.</p>
</text>
